4. Detach task profile from origin_availability_alpha (makes profile available).

5. Attach task profile to destination_availability_alpha.
6. Confirm candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha.
(Now destination has link, origin prepared but no link.)

7. Activate origin node (requires candidate_prepared origin, route_task_profile_alpha). We have origin prepared true, route_task_profile_alpha available? After step4 we detached, making profile available. So we can use it for activation. Good.

8. Activate destination node (requires candidate_prepared destination, route_task_profile_alpha). Destination prepared true, profile still linked to destination (so not available). However activation action does not require route_task_profile_available, just takes it as parameter; it does not change its availability. So we can still use the profile even if it's linked? The precondition does not check availability. So we can still pass the profile as argument even if it's linked to destination. That's fine. So we can activate destination node using the same profile while it's linked to destination. Good.

Thus we don't need to detach destination's link before activation.

Now after activation, we have nodes ready.

9. Load origin payload.
10. Load destination payload.
11. Unload origin payload.
12. Unload destination payload.

Now we have origin/destination locked and confirmed, nodes occupied and ready.

13. Assemble transport leg (requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available). All true.

14. Authorize transport leg loading (requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha, not transport_leg_loading_authorized). At this point origin_availability_alpha does NOT have task profile linked (we detached earlier). So we need to link it again temporarily. So before authorization, we need to attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha again.

Thus we need to attach profile to origin (step13a), then authorize (step14), then detach origin's profile again (step15) if we want to keep destination's link only.

But note: after we attach profile to origin for authorization, we will have origin linked again; we must ensure that we don't break any precondition for later actions (none require origin not linked). So we can attach, authorize, detach.

Now we need to ensure that after we detach origin's link, the transport_leg_loading_authorized remains true (it's not affected). Good.

Now we need to mark dispatch ready for origin and destination (requires origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized). We have those after step14.

Now we need to allocate dispatch slot for origin, then dispatch shift, then dispatch origin.

But we must consider that dispatch_slot_alpha is currently linked to shift_candidate_alpha (from init) and not available. We need to make it available by dispatching shift first.

Thus order: after we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized, we can dispatch shift (which will make slot available). Then allocate slot to origin, then dispatch origin.

