But note: dispatching shift will also make vehicle_unit_gamma available and dispatch_slot_available. After we allocate slot to origin, slot becomes not available; after we dispatch origin, slot becomes available again (goal). Good.

Now we need to ensure that after we dispatch shift, we still have transport_leg_assembled etc unaffected. Dispatch shift does not affect those.

Now we need to ensure that after we dispatch origin, we still have transport_leg_assembled etc (they remain). Dispatch origin does not affect them.

Now we need to ensure that we still have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha after dispatch (effect does not remove it). So goal satisfied.

Now we need to verify that we haven't inadvertently removed any needed links like candidate_origin_availability_linked shift_candidate_alpha etc. Not needed.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently removed candidate_vehicle_linked etc. Not.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently removed cargo_available; after load/unload cycles cargo ends available (true). Good.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently removed compliance_certificate_available; we released it at step1, and we never linked it again. So remains available.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently removed operator_available; we never assigned operator, so remains available.

